          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.146
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In Fig. 1.2, the equalities are between two angles and the non-included side of the two triangles. This condition is referred to as the "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "AAS (Angle Angle Side)",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " condition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.147,
            0.759,
            0.166
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "As we have seen, the AAS condition guarantees congruence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.166,
            0.848,
            0.225
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have seen that the SSA condition doesn’t always guarantee congruence. However, there are some special cases when SSA does guarantee congruence. Here is one such important case."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.241,
            0.648,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measuring Two Sides in a Right Triangle"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.266,
            0.846,
            0.308
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ ΔABC and ΔXYZ are right-angled triangles such that "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "BC = YZ = 4"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " cm, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\angle \\mathrm{B} = \\angle \\mathrm{Y} = 90^{\\circ}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and AC = XZ=5cm. Are they congruent?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.327,
            0.847,
            0.368
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Can there exist non-congruent triangles having these measurements? Construct and find out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.39,
            0.787,
            0.411
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Looking at the rough diagram helps in planning the construction."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.373,
            0.419,
            0.625,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
